{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #500: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. What is $\\mathrm{ex}_3(n,K_4^3)$? That is, the largest number of $3$-edges which can placed on $n$ vertices so that there exists no $K_4^3$, a set of 4 vertices which is covered by all 4 possible $3$-edges. Current best: The current best upper bound is\\[\\mathrm{ex}_3(n,K_4^3)\\leq 0.5611666\\binom{n}{3},\\]due to Razborov \\cite{Ra10}. Prize: $500. OEIS: A140462. Tags: graph theory, hypergraphs, turan number."},"claim_id":"vcl_f123681de294eb1f4bdeb79fc102a217bf3da5c2f180cd8b8c66140b446a0cdf","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:500","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_8b6c28a1f2e6cb30","object_root":"sha256:642917e84086f7e94bbb663b6c9bba450868b3e01758c1195619c6c24bf7e7f7","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:500"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}